ON-PREMISE ALLOCATION IMPLEMENTATION (Session 3 - Addendum)
================================================================================

Date: 2025-10-03
Issue: On-premise allocation was missing from initial implementation

PROBLEM IDENTIFIED:
- Initial implementation only handled cloud (reserved + on-demand)
- On-premise instances completely skipped
- Violates SeisSol pattern of cluster-based allocation

ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS:
HPO has different cost structure than SeisSol:
- SeisSol: On-prem always cheapest → Exclusive on-prem priority
- HPO Cost Ranking:
  1. Cloud Reserved g4dn: $0.503/hour (CHEAPEST)
  2. Cloud Reserved g5: $0.80/hour
  3. On-Premise g5: $0.90/hour (MID-TIER, not cheapest!)
  4. Cloud On-Demand g4dn: $0.798/hour
  5. Cloud On-Demand g5: $1.28/hour (MOST EXPENSIVE)

CORRECT STRATEGY (SeisSol Pattern Adapted):
1. Try on-prem FIRST (if can fully allocate)
   - If successful → Workflow locks to on-prem cluster
   - If insufficient → Skip on-prem, use cloud only
2. Use cloud resources (reserved + on-demand)
   - Workflow locks to cloud cluster
3. NO MIXING of on-prem + cloud in single workflow

CLUSTER ISOLATION RULES:
- On-prem workflows: Scale ONLY within on-prem (all iterations)
- Cloud workflows: Scale ONLY within cloud (reserved + on-demand)
- NO cross-cluster migration (on-prem ↔ cloud)

